# core/provenance - Where did this come from?
#
# Answers: the source file, converter agent and version, conversion timestamps and
# editorial metadata behind the model that contains the focus element.
#
# Does NOT prove: that the source model is current, correct, or approved. It
# records how the RDF came to exist. A conversion at 09:43 says the file was read
# then, not that the architecture was true then.
#
# Run this for every material claim in an answer. An architecture statement without
# a source is an assertion; with one it is evidence, and the reader can go and look
# at the model themselves.
#
# Three shape decisions, each forced by real converter output:
#
# The model is found through {{MEMBERSHIP:focus}}, so HOW membership is expressed is
# a profile fact rather than a decision baked in here. This template used to hard-code
# co-location, which is correct for pre-1.3 output and returns nothing on 1.3, where
# the model resource is not in the element's graph at all. The three modes a profile
# can declare:
#
#   same-graph-colocation  the element's semantic graph declares its model. Default,
#                          because it holds for every converter at default flags.
#   bounded-folder-tree    walk part_of upward. Only for stores whose folder chain is
#                          complete; the ArchiMate and C4 chains break where BPMN's holds.
#   direct-predicate       one hop along arch:inModel. The 1.3 contract, and better
#                          than both: no graph co-location and no folder walk needed.
#
# FILTER EXISTS anchors the element to the graph without binding its predicates,
# which would otherwise return one duplicate row per property. It is what carries
# co-location's join, and is harmlessly redundant under direct-predicate, where the
# membership edge anchors the element itself.
#
# The source file is read through a UNION because converters disagree about where
# it lives: BPMN, Structurizr and Backstage put dct:source on the model, while
# ArchiMate puts it only on the prov:Entity the model was derived from.
#
# Each lookup carries its OWN graph scope and its own required triple. Collapsing
# them into one scope holding a chain of OPTIONALs is the obvious simplification and
# silently returns nothing: with no required pattern, the group has nothing to
# anchor the join to. That failure was observed, not theorised.
#
# An element from a model converted without a provenance graph returns the model
# row with empty columns. Report that as missing evidence rather than passing over
# it.
#
# More than one row for one element is not a fault. A model can carry two
# generation times that mean different things - the date an author declared for the
# export and the moment the converter ran - and LeanIX output does. Read both: an
# export taken days before it was converted is a staleness signal worth reporting,
# and collapsing the two would hide it.
#
# Parameters: FOCUS_IRI, LIMIT
# DISTINCT because the source UNION has two branches and some converters satisfy
# both, which would otherwise report the same file twice - once per branch - and
# read as two sources.
{{PREFIXES}}
SELECT DISTINCT ?model ?source ?generated ?startedAt ?agentName ?agentVersion ?title ?creator
WHERE {
  {{GRAPH_OPEN:semantic}}
    VALUES ?focus { {{FOCUS_IRI}} }
    {{MEMBERSHIP:focus}}
    FILTER EXISTS { ?focus ?anchorPredicate ?anchorObject }
  {{GRAPH_CLOSE}}
  OPTIONAL {
    {{GRAPH_OPEN:provenance}}
      { ?model {{ROLE:source_file}} ?source }
      UNION
      { ?model {{ROLE:derived_from}} ?entity . ?entity {{ROLE:source_file}} ?source }
    {{GRAPH_CLOSE}}
  }
  OPTIONAL {
    {{GRAPH_OPEN:provenance}}
      ?model {{ROLE:generated_at}} ?generated .
    {{GRAPH_CLOSE}}
  }
  OPTIONAL {
    {{GRAPH_OPEN:provenance}}
      ?model {{ROLE:generated_by}} ?activity .
      ?activity prov:startedAtTime ?startedAt .
    {{GRAPH_CLOSE}}
  }
  OPTIONAL {
    {{GRAPH_OPEN:provenance}}
      ?model {{ROLE:generated_by}} ?agentActivity .
      ?agentActivity prov:wasAssociatedWith ?agent .
      ?agent {{ROLE:agent_name}} ?agentName .
      OPTIONAL { ?agent {{ROLE:agent_version}} ?agentVersion }
    {{GRAPH_CLOSE}}
  }
  OPTIONAL {
    {{GRAPH_OPEN:provenance}}
      ?model dct:title ?title .
    {{GRAPH_CLOSE}}
  }
  OPTIONAL {
    {{GRAPH_OPEN:provenance}}
      ?model dct:creator ?creator .
    {{GRAPH_CLOSE}}
  }
}
LIMIT {{LIMIT}}
